course: dictionary
lesson: 574
title: Austrian: a word for a place and its people
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Austrian can be an adjective or a noun. Austria is a country in central Europe, with mountains called the Alps. Something Austrian comes from Austria or is connected with it, like «the Austrian Alps».
explain: An Austrian is a person from Austria. Austria is the place and Austrian is the word for the people and things from it. Always start Austria and Austrian with a capital letter.
explain: Context shows you which job the word is doing. In «Mozart is a famous Austrian composer», Austrian describes Mozart, so it is an adjective. In «An Austrian sang at the concert», it names a person, so it is a noun. Try swapping in «a person from Austria» to check your meaning.
fact: Austria is a landlocked country, which means it has no coastline by the sea.
fact: The capital of Austria is Vienna, and most people there speak German.
fact: Mozart, a famous composer of music, was Austrian.
fact: «The Sound of Music» is a famous story set in Austria, with its mountains and the Alps.
fact: In the 1800s, the Austrian Empire included Galicia, a land that is part of today's Ukraine.
exercise: «Mozart is a famous Austrian composer.» What does Austrian tell us about Mozart? | He lives in Scotland | He plays the drums | He is a writer of stories | *He comes from Austria
exercise: «The Austrian Alps are covered in snow in winter.» Where are these mountains? | In Scotland | In Australia | Under the sea | *In Austria
exercise: Find the word that means a person from Austria. | Vienna | *An Austrian | Germany | Alps
test: What is the capital city of Austria? | Edinburgh | Berlin | Paris | *Vienna
test: «The Sound of Music» is set in which country? | *Austria | Scotland | Ukraine | Australia
exam: Which sentence uses Austrian as a noun? | «The Austrian Empire was large.» | *«An Austrian sang at the concert.» | «Austrian German is spoken there.» | «The Austrian Alps are high.»
